%I A400586 #26 Oct 11 2026 09:33:36
%S A400586 1,2,13,23,58,47,128,129,211,220,232,213,235,264,317,277,350,390,393,
%T A400586 353,386,427,491,460,474,495,540,529,534,636,682,599,625,779,837,722,
%U A400586 799,865,964,857,906,1035,1096,965,1026,1147,1208,1097,1178,1279,1360,1269
%N A400586 Paired Comma Sequence: Interlaced pair of sequences of positive numbers with the property that, for each sequence in the pair, the sequence formed by the pairs of digits adjacent to the commas between the terms is the same as the successive differences between each term and the previous term of the other sequence, and starting with a(1) = 1 and b(1) = 2.
%C A400586 Sequence and description adapted from the comma sequence (A121805).
%C A400586 Shown interlaced here, but "commas between the terms" relies on the sequences not being interlaced (see Example).
%C A400586 Starting with a(1) = 1 and b(1) = 2, there are 20250 member pairs. The final pair, 939484 and 999956, prevents the generation of a new pair.
%H A400586 Brady Haran and Neil J. A. Sloane, <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=A020pGO5MBs">The Immortal Kangaroo Sequence</a>, Numberphile video (2026).
%H A400586 Joshua Morley, <a href="/A400586/a400586_1.txt">Python Program</a>
%e A400586 Consider the first three pairs of terms (deinterlaced):
%e A400586   1,13,58
%e A400586   2,23,47
%e A400586 The first "1" concatenated with the "1" from 13 makes 11. Add that to the first term of the second sequence, 2, to get the second term of the first sequence: 13.
%e A400586 The first "2" concatenated with the "2" from 23 makes 22. Add that to the first term of the first sequence, 1, to get the second term of the second sequence: 23.
%e A400586 The "3" from "13" concatenated with the "5" from 58 makes 35. Add that to the second term of the second sequence, 23, to get the third term of the first sequence: 58.
%e A400586 The "3" from "23" concatenated with the "4" from "47" makes 34. Add that to the second term of the first sequence, 13, to get the third term of the second sequence: 47.
%o A400586 (Python) # see linked program
%Y A400586 Cf. A121805.
%K A400586 base,nonn,fini,new
%O A400586 1,2
